! fp_to_memory_laar.strap -- LFT IS A "TO MEMORY" OPERATION, ITS $R
! OPERAND WAITS FOR THE ONE LAAR, AND AN INDEXED M+ INTO INDEX STORAGE
! PREPARES IN SERIES AFTER THE DECODE HOLD.  Built 2026-11-17
! (docs/atlas_oracle.md, "Closing the residuals" item 10).
!
! THE SOURCES (read in the page images).
!  - Perf. Char. Vol. 1 printed p.3-20 (PDF 38): "$Z, $IA, $MB, and $RM,
!    $FT and $TR are bona fide main memory locations"; the I-box "uses
!    the LAAR to store the internal operand address".
!  - Vol. 1 printed p.3-21 (PDF 39): "Since there is only one LAAR ... a
!    wait must occur until the LAAR is free for reloading. ...
!    Measurements on consecutive floating-point-to-memory operations
!    (ST, MT, LFT, etc.) do not therefore yield realistic timing";
!    "A store into index storage is a time-consuming operation ... the
!    I-box does no further decoding until the new index contents
!    arrives."
!  - Vol. 2 printed 34D (PDF 41): pp. 61, 92 (LFT) "refer to 'to memory'
!    operations"; repeated ones "lead to queuing for the LAAR".
!  - Vol. 2 PDF 69 (printed 62): M+ into $X9-$X12 7.86 us unindexed,
!    9.07 indexed (4 clocks); PDF 99 (printed 92): LFT 4.36 us from
!    memory, 4.06 from $X9, 6.76 from $R.
!
! THE BODY.  $X5 = 0 and $X9 = the FP one.  Six M+(U) into $X9 unindexed
! (the CONTROL block for the indexed preparation), six indexed by $X5,
! eight LFT(U) from memory, $R = the FP one by TI, eight LFT(U) from $R.
! The value check is FT, word 14: LFT places its operand there with FT
! bits 61-63 zero (Ref. Manual p.98), so it holds the FP one's word,
! 0028000000000000 hex.  The M+ sums are not checked: this deck is a
! timing deck, and the accumulator is the one throughout.
!
! MEASURED, 2026-11-17 (CYCLES in run_tests.sh's run line).
!   the model as of this deck .......................... 776
!   OBSERVED INJECTIONS, each reverted from a saved copy checked with cmp
!   (FT and PC pass in every one):
!   - fpLaarStore without LFT (no LAAR for LFT) ......... FAIL cycles 656
!   - intFrom = eboxDoneAt ($R not waiting for the LAAR) FAIL cycles 738
!   - serialNow = 0 (no serial preparation) ............. FAIL cycles 752
!     (24 clocks = 4 a copy over the six indexed M+)
!   - lftDeferredLaar False (LFT gated at its load) ..... FAIL cycles 846
!   Nothing else failed.  The control is decks/fp_internal_operand.strap
!   (L from $R with no FP store before it), which stays at 208 under all
!   four.  No existing CYCLES pin in run_tests.sh moved with the change.

        SLC, (8)2000.0

START   LX, $X5, ZERO
        L(BU,64,8), FONE           ! the FP one, as a VFL word
        ST(BU,64,8), $X9           ! into $X9's word in index storage
        L(U), FONE                 ! the accumulator = one
        M+(U), $X9
        M+(U), $X9
        M+(U), $X9
        M+(U), $X9
        M+(U), $X9
        M+(U), $X9
        M+(U), $X9($X5)
        M+(U), $X9($X5)
        M+(U), $X9($X5)
        M+(U), $X9($X5)
        M+(U), $X9($X5)
        M+(U), $X9($X5)
        LFT(U), FONE
        LFT(U), FONE
        LFT(U), FONE
        LFT(U), FONE
        LFT(U), FONE
        LFT(U), FONE
        LFT(U), FONE
        LFT(U), FONE
        TI, 1, FONE, 9.0           ! $R = the FP one
        LFT(U), $R
        LFT(U), $R
        LFT(U), $R
        LFT(U), $R
        LFT(U), $R
        LFT(U), $R
        LFT(U), $R
        LFT(U), $R

PASS    BEW, $

        SLC, (8)2200.0

ZERO    DD(BU,64,8), 0
FONE    DD(BU,64,8), (16)0028000000000000

        END, START
